WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.168
[intense music]

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.037
RICKO: I'm learning a
new country this winter

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.740
so my greatest challenge
is don't let the land

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.743
or the weather kill me.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.745
[hopeful music]

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:14.714
[wind howling]

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.716
[water rushing]

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.753
SKYLER: The water is cold.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.955
RICKO: Your feet will get
used to it after a while.

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:31.197
SKYLER: This is a
big chunk of ice.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.866
NARRATOR: Ricko and
Skyler have traveled

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.135
to the Selawik Hot Springs
with plans to break

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.270
trail for vital resources.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.739
But with potentially
catastrophic flooding

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.708
underneath the cabins
on the grounds,

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.877
the duo must act
quickly to ensure

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.678
the safety of the structures.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.380
If they are unable
to stop the water

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:52.552
from damaging the foundations,
the cabins won't last.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.021
[pensive music]

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.423
RICKO: It warmed
up out here today

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.058
so gave us a little
opportunity to start working

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.261
on this water situation.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.497
Basically got the flood plain
by creating a channel of all

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:07.834
this water going over the dam
and alongside of the cabin

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.569
instead of through the cabin.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.806
All this grass and moss was
insulating the warm rocks

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.841
and mud at the bottom so
when it gets real cold,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.509
it's freezing all the
way to the bottom,

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.746
creating a huge
flood plain out here.

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:22.849
What I'm trying to do is
break away all this moss,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:27.654
grass, willows, roots, expose
that warm rocks and mud

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.856
and hopefully that
keeps it from freezing

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.258
down and just has
a natural creek

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.993
to flow through all winter.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.396
And it's basically a Band-Aid
though because once it gets

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.431
real cold, it might freeze
all the way down again

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:41.501
and create this whole flood
plain to start up again.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:44.103
Eventually that beaver
house has to be destroyed.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.540
So there's no water flowing
around or next to the cabins

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.578
at all and just no hope for a
flood plain happening again.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.679
[water rushing]

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.581
People out here, we
depend on these cabins

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.784
and we depend on it every
year for generations.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:00.620
We let these cabins get
eliminated by water and ice,

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.889
that could easily eliminate
someone's life that's coming

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.158
out here unprepared thinking
they have a nice spot

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.460
to get cozy in and dry off in.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.896
Not only that, there's water
over the snow machine trail

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.764
and if you go in that
thing and you get hurt,

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.333
end up in the water,
and you come in

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.302
and the cabins are glaciered
over with ice and water,

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.337
you're in a bad spot.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.138
[dramatic music]

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.106
[water rushing]

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.509
There is a mysterious
black bird.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.710
[pensive music]

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.778
First time we're seeing
them was when I was a kid.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.679
[water rushing]

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.147
It has this pointed beak.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:32.285
It doesn't have webbed feet,
but it swims, it dives,

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.888
it hunts fish way up
here in the headwaters.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.890
It dries itself off
in the snow and then

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.124
it hangs out in the trees.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.959
It's unique only to these areas.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.562
I really don't even know if
that bird's been discovered yet.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.398
If there's no name for that
bird and it's a new one,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:47.033
it's going to be De Wilde bird.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.436
[water rushing]

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.340
OK, let's check it out.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.576
Damn, look at this.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.845
There's no more water
going underneath the cabin.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.913
[water sounds]

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.282
Oof.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.182
Yeah, remember this?

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.618
It was just flowing right here.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.021
This will help out a lot.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.023
All this driving over
with the snow machine

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.090
was a big ol' deal.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.492
Woah.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.060
All this is hanging ice now.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.895
[pensive music]

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:20.133
Check out the snow machine
trail and as you can see,

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.569
the water has quit flowing.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.438
Dude, the trail looks
a whole lot better.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.840
Real gratifying feeling
basically saving

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:31.811
cabins by playing in a
puddle so a little tired now.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.646
I'm glad we got the job done.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.816
Let's go inside, take a break.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.818
We want to bed early.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.520
Tomorrow, we have a
lot of work to do.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.559
[upbeat music]

